# BGE-M3 Dense Encoder Ablation

Status: concluded on 2026-09-07.

## Objective

Determine whether replacing frozen EmbeddingGemma document embeddings with frozen BGE-M3 dense embeddings improves the existing signed-difference linear classifier.

## Compared Pipelines

```text
EmbeddingGemma: Eᴿ − Eᴶ ∈ ℝ⁷⁶⁸  → linear classifier → 3 logits
BGE-M3:        Eᴿ − Eᴶ ∈ ℝ¹⁰²⁴ → linear classifier → 3 logits
```

Both experiments use fold 0, the same outer-test rows, the same inner partition, class-weighted cross-entropy, AdamW, seed 42, 50 epochs, patience 50, and checkpoint selection by validation loss.

BGE-M3 uses its native 8,192-token context and no prompt. EmbeddingGemma uses a 2,048-token context and its sentence-similarity prompt. Consequently, this is a comparison of each encoder under its intended dense encoding contract, not a tokenizer-and-context-controlled model swap.

## Reproduce

```bash { name=train-bge-linear-fold-zero }
cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/ml"
.venv/bin/python scripts/train_classifier.py \
  --feature-report artifacts/data__bge_m3_pair_features.json \
  --report artifacts/train__bge_m3_linear_classifier.json \
  --device cuda \
  --fold 0 \
  --max-epochs 50 \
  --patience 50 \
  --experiment resume-jd-linear-bge-m3
```

```bash { name=evaluate-bge-representations }
cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/ml"
.venv/bin/python scripts/evaluate_classifier.py \
  --training-report artifacts/train__bge_m3_linear_classifier.json \
  --feature-report artifacts/data__bge_m3_pair_features.json \
  --fold 0 \
  --report artifacts/eval__bge_m3_representation.json
```

