## Outer-Test Comparison

| Metric | EmbeddingGemma | BGE-M3 | BGE-M3 delta |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| Accuracy | 0.4785 | 0.4798 | +0.0013 |
| Macro F1 | 0.3787 | 0.3798 | +0.0011 |
| Pre-training 10-neighbor label purity | 0.7604 | 0.7195 | -0.0409 |
| Pre-training silhouette score | -0.0491 | -0.0271 | +0.0221 |
| Post-training 10-neighbor label purity | 0.6122 | 0.6113 | -0.0009 |
| Post-training silhouette score | -0.0476 | -0.0158 | +0.0318 |

The changes in accuracy and macro F1 are approximately one tenth of one percentage point. This run does not show a meaningful classification improvement from replacing EmbeddingGemma with BGE-M3 dense embeddings.

## BGE-M3 Held-Out Classification

| Class | Precision | Recall | F1 | Support |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| No Fit | 0.8437 | 0.5114 | 0.6368 | 7,802 |
| Potential Fit | 0.2593 | 0.3372 | 0.2932 | 2,079 |
| Good Fit | 0.1295 | 0.5452 | 0.2093 | 763 |

BGE-M3 improves Potential Fit F1 relative to the EmbeddingGemma run but reduces Good Fit F1. The net macro-F1 change is negligible.

## Representation Metrics

| BGE-M3 metric | Before training | After training |
| --- | ---: | ---: |
| 10-neighbor label purity | 0.7195 | 0.6113 |
| Silhouette score | -0.0271 | -0.0158 |
| Intra-class cosine similarity | 0.0136 | 0.0427 |
| Inter-class cosine similarity | 0.0086 | -0.0338 |
| Cosine separation | 0.0050 | 0.0764 |
| t-SNE trustworthiness | 0.9991 | 0.9993 |

## Plot

```text
data/analysis/09269d4a89194ed89f68f82ce29f4560/fold_0/tsne_before_after.png
```

The pre-training t-SNE forms many compact islands, but all three labels remain mixed inside them. The post-training logit projection also remains label-mixed. As in the EmbeddingGemma experiment, the independently fitted t-SNE panels cannot be compared by absolute position or global shape; the neighborhood and classification metrics provide the comparison.

## Decision

Do not replace EmbeddingGemma with BGE-M3 solely for this dense signed-difference classifier. The measured outer-test accuracy and macro F1 are effectively unchanged, while BGE-M3 requires a larger checkpoint and longer embedding runtime.

This result evaluates only BGE-M3's single dense vector. It does not evaluate BGE-M3 sparse retrieval or multi-vector late interaction, and therefore does not determine whether those representations are useful for resume-JD matching.
